00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:39,809
The whole agent run invoke_agent
took around 6,000 milliseconds.

138
00:10:40,447 --> 00:10:47,896
Inside it, first LLM call It
takes around 1,900 milliseconds

139
00:10:48,403 --> 00:10:51,682
and close to about 2,500 tokens.

140
00:10:51,950 --> 00:10:57,657
In 34 out and it finishes with tools_use.

141
00:10:58,208 --> 00:10:59,955
The model decides to call a tool.

142
00:11:01,354 --> 00:11:07,003
The tool estimates_repair_cost
come back in 30 milliseconds

143
00:11:07,254 --> 00:11:08,488
with service unavailable.

144
00:11:09,114 --> 00:11:09,660
It fail.

145
00:11:10,956 --> 00:11:14,593
The second LLM call reads that
failure and decides to retry.

146
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:20,081
Then the same tool runs again in under
millisecond, and this time it succeed.

147
00:11:21,075 --> 00:11:25,737
The third LLM call writes the
answer and finish the loop.

148
00:11:26,905 --> 00:11:28,032
Two things to notice.

149
00:11:28,304 --> 00:11:31,825
One, almost all six second
is the model thinking.

150
00:11:33,278 --> 00:11:35,223
The tools take milliseconds.

151
00:11:36,151 --> 00:11:40,612
If you want to make this agent faster,
the tools are not where you look.

152
00:11:42,094 --> 00:11:46,540
Second, you can see the agent
recover, a failed tool call, a

153
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,425
